The legal text is the Constitution of the Central African Republic of 30 August 2023, as printed in the Journal
officiel de la République centrafricaine (JORCA, special issue no 9, 4 September 2023).

The Central African Republic publishes no official online copy. The bytes here come from a third-party host: the
Digithèque MJP (Jean-Pierre Maury, Université de Perpignan), page https://mjp.univ-perp.fr/constit/cf2023.htm, which
gives the Journal officiel as its source. The same page is also held in print form by FAO FAOLEX
(https://faolex.fao.org/docs/pdf/caf233696.pdf). Credit for the bytes: Digithèque MJP, Université de Perpignan.
The words were not changed; spelling and typographical slips of the printed text are kept. The text was only split
into files and lines.

Why it may be published: the Central African Republic is a member of the African Intellectual Property Organization
(OAPI) and applies Annex VII (literary and artistic property) of the Bangui Agreement. Article 6 of Annex VII
("Objets non protégés") says:

  "La protection prévue par la présente partie de l'Annexe ne s'étend pas : i) Aux textes officiels de nature
  législative, administrative ou judiciaire, ni à leurs traductions officielles ; ii) Aux nouvelles du jour ; et,
  iii) Aux simples faits et données."

(Bangui Agreement, Act of 14 December 2015, official OAPI text, http://siege.oapi.int/Ressources/accord_bangui/2020/francais.pdf.)
The Constitution is an official text of a legislative nature, so it carries no copyright. The page of the host states
no reuse terms that we found.

The Code pénal (loi n° 10.001 du 6 janvier 2010 portant Code pénal centrafricain) is copied from the copy held by
WIPO Lex, record CF003 (https://wipolex-res.wipo.int/edocs/lexdocs/laws/fr/cf/cf003fr.pdf), retrieved on 30 October
2026. Credit for the bytes: WIPO Lex. It is an official text of a legislative nature, so Article 6(i) of Annex VII
(quoted above) applies to it too.

The Code du travail (loi n° 09.004 du 29 janvier 2009 portant Code du travail de la République centrafricaine) is
copied from the Journal officiel de la République centrafricaine, special edition of 7 September 2010, in the PDF
held by FAO FAOLEX (https://faolex.fao.org/docs/pdf/caf158592.pdf), retrieved on 30 October 2026. It is an official
text of a legislative nature, so Article 6(i) of Annex VII (quoted above) applies to it too.

The Code de procédure pénale (loi n° 10.002 du 6 janvier 2010) is copied from the transcription published by Equipo
Nizkor / Derechos Human Rights (https://www.derechos.org/intlaw/doc/caf2.html), which gives the Journal officiel
special edition of 15 January 2010 as its source, retrieved on 30 October 2026. Credit for the bytes: Equipo Nizkor.
It is an official text of a legislative nature, so Article 6(i) of Annex VII (quoted above) applies to it too.

